   "final_text": "All four events in the feed are handled, and the feed has been quiet for about 50 minutes with nothing left pending.\n\n**1. Noah Patel moved from Software Engineer to Sales Rep (case-82f1c080, effective 2026-11-02)**\n- **Access:** I removed his engineering access (Eng-Git and VPN-Users) and added Sales-CRM. He kept All-Staff. Policy allows no overlap between old and new access, so he never held both sets at once. The new group set passed the segregation-of-duties check.\n- **Finance:** I changed his cost center from CC-1000 to CC-3000 (the Finance code for Workday's \"CC-3000 Sales\"). His expense approver is now his new manager, Noah Okafor. He had no expense reports in flight.\n\n**2\u20134. Manager changed from Owen Iyer to Noah Okafor for Noah Patel, Mateo Nguyen and Leila Fischer (case-0575665b, case-94c16aad, case-97623f40)**\n- **Approvers:** Noah Patel's approver was already updated under case 1. I set Mateo's and Leila's approver to Noah Okafor.\n- **Pending report:** Leila had one report waiting for approval (exp-e5e138e2, $170). Changing an approver doesn't move reports already waiting, so I sent it to Okafor myself.\n- **Why I changed each person separately:** I didn't move Owen's whole approval list in one step. Owen also approves Noah Okafor's own expenses, and moving everyone would have made Okafor his own approver. Owen still approves Okafor, which is correct.\n\nNo owning team needed to fix anything and nothing needed a human decision, so I didn't open any requests or escalations."
